Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think it's interesting to emphasize that the revenues of DOE are predominantly from Malampaya Gas Fund.

asr-000202
00:31:10.140 --> 00:31:16.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then from 2026 to 2027, it's still very high, almost to the 2023 levels.

asr-000203
00:31:17.660 --> 00:31:19.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then your others, what are they?

asr-000204
00:31:20.720 --> 00:31:22.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What are your other sources?

asr-000205
00:31:23.400 --> 00:31:25.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Other like fee permits.

asr-000206
00:31:25.200 --> 00:31:25.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So basically…

asr-000207
00:31:25.940 --> 00:31:27.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Basically, fee permits, no?

asr-000208
00:31:27.560 --> 00:31:29.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So talagang ang laking bagay nung sa Malampaya.

asr-000209
00:31:30.040 --> 00:31:33.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Of course, I have to say that because ako'y nag-sponsor niyan and pinaglaban natin niyan.

asr-000210
00:31:34.280 --> 00:31:38.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And in fact, 2028 will likely go up because of the new discovery.

asr-000211
00:31:39.040 --> 00:31:39.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, that's good.

asr-000212
00:31:39.940 --> 00:31:40.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000213
00:31:42.320 --> 00:31:43.020
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Next slide.

asr-000214
00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:55.020
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: For fiscal year 2027, the DOE's total proposed budget is 5.58 billion, reflecting an increase of 1.14 billion or 25.7%.

asr-000215
00:31:55.940 --> 00:32:01.220
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Compared with fiscal year 2026 GA of 4.43 billion.

asr-000216
00:32:01.220 --> 00:32:20.220
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: From 2022 to 2026, new appropriations generally maintained the largest share in the DOE's total budget, from 59.4 to 68.9%, versus automatic appropriations of about 31.1 to 40.6%.

asr-000217
00:32:20.220 --> 00:32:25.220
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: But for 2027, new appropriations decreased by ₱935 million.

asr-000218
00:32:25.940 --> 00:32:36.780
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: And account for only 36.4% of the total recommended budget, while 63.6% comes from the SAGF.

asr-000219
00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:50.740
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: In other words, the department's budgetary requirements will be heavily supported through the SAGF, sourced from the revenues from energy service contracts and other collections of the department.

asr-000220
00:32:51.740 --> 00:32:54.020
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: This chart shows the DOE…

asr-000221
00:32:54.020 --> 00:32:55.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Before you leave again, I just want to comment.

asr-000222
00:32:55.940 --> 00:33:16.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, for the first time since 2022, which is the last six years, the new appropriations will actually be less.

asr-000223
00:33:17.480 --> 00:33:25.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: This is very important because basically, DOE is more self-sustaining than you were in the past.

asr-000224
00:33:25.240 --> 00:33:28.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I think compared to many other agencies, malaking bagay yun na.

asr-000225
00:33:28.740 --> 00:33:30.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, it's really something that I wanted to emphasize.

asr-000226
00:33:31.400 --> 00:33:38.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And as you said, the reason is, meron kayong revenues na pumapasok to support this.

asr-000227
00:33:38.880 --> 00:33:40.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I want to emphasize this because it's a good thing.

asr-000228
00:33:41.140 --> 00:33:42.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hirap naman ang puro bad news.

asr-000229
00:33:42.320 --> 00:33:43.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, may good news naman tayo.

asr-000230
00:33:43.620 --> 00:33:44.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: If you want to add, Secretary?

asr-000231
00:33:44.800 --> 00:33:53.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I wanted to add also, hindi pa nabibilang diyan the contributions of our GOCCs because, for example, PSALM is one of the highest contributors in dividends.

asr-000232
00:33:53.340 --> 00:33:54.340
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: I think just this…

asr-000233
00:33:55.240 --> 00:33:56.980
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: This year is about P30 billion.

asr-000234
00:33:58.280 --> 00:33:59.580
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Magkano ba yung contribution mo?

asr-000235
00:34:01.180 --> 00:34:03.600
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Good afternoon, Senator Pia.

asr-000236
00:34:04.260 --> 00:34:06.980
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: Secretary, our contribution for this year is about P4 billion.

asr-000237
00:34:07.160 --> 00:34:10.000
PSALM President and CEO Dennis Edward de la Serna: For next year, we're projecting around P30 plus billion.

asr-000238
00:34:11.380 --> 00:34:13.560
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: So, the others are also contributing.

asr-000239
00:34:13.720 --> 00:34:17.840
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Pero wala siya dyan kasi this is remittance lang sa katina.

asr-000240
00:34:18.200 --> 00:34:19.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay. Thank you. Go ahead.

asr-000241
00:34:19.920 --> 00:34:20.640
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Next slide.

asr-000242
00:34:20.640 --> 00:34:20.720
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Next slide.

asr-000243
00:34:21.240 --> 00:34:24.600
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: This chart shows the DOE's budget utilization rate.

asr-000244
00:34:25.240 --> 00:34:28.100
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: From 2022 to 31 August 2026.

asr-000245
00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:40.680
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Upon completion of procurement of the mobile energy system and the DOE automation project, which are already undergoing procurement, the obligation rate will increase to 67%.

asr-000246
00:34:40.680 --> 00:34:48.160
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: The DOE expects to reach at least 95.89% utilization rate for 2026.

asr-000247
00:34:48.600 --> 00:34:54.860
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: The increase in the DOE's recommended 2027 budget from the current year's budget level.

asr-000248
00:34:55.240 --> 00:34:59.820
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: It's in large part owing to increased funding for these three major projects.

asr-000249
00:34:59.820 --> 00:35:18.560
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: The Philippine Gradiometry and Seismic Survey Project, or simply the Gradiometry Project, the Mobile Energy Systems, or MES, under the Total Electrification Project, and the ISSP, which includes the DOE Automation Project.

asr-000250
00:35:18.920 --> 00:35:25.120
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: The Gradiometry Project is the department’s initiative to improve resource mapping and prospect

asr-000251
00:35:25.240 --> 00:35:25.820
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: identification,

asr-000252
00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:38.220
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Reduce exploration risk and help attract greater upstream energy investments in the Philippines by generating higher quality geophysical data across priority petroleum basins.

asr-000253
00:35:38.940 --> 00:35:42.780
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: The Grid Geometry Project covers 120,000 square kilometers.

asr-000254
00:35:43.620 --> 00:35:48.900
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: The area could support up to 120 individual exploration service contracts.

asr-000255
00:35:48.900 --> 00:35:52.780
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Using data from the recently awarded exploration contracts,

asr-000256
00:35:53.360 --> 00:35:55.220
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: just 10% of

asr-000257
00:35:55.220 --> 00:36:04.740
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: the potential 120 contracts alone would already account for approximately ₱16.8 billion of potential private-sector investments.

asr-000258
00:36:04.740 --> 00:36:09.740
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: And that is not even counting potential oil and gas discoveries.

asr-000259
00:36:11.120 --> 00:36:17.680
DOE Undersecretary Giovanni Carlo J. Bacordo: Under the Total Electrification Project, the department is procuring MES that will provide...

asr-000260
00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:23.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: One last before you go to that again, let's go back to this because I was very interested in this when it was presented.

asr-000261
00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:30.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The Philippine Gradiometry and Seismic Survey Project investment is ₱2.7 billion.

asr-000262
00:36:31.040 --> 00:36:35.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And that's basically to be surveying that area that was blocked off.

asr-000263
00:36:35.500 --> 00:36:40.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I think, Secretary, you explained that even the selection of the area,

asr-000264
00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:45.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because it's costly to survey the whole area, is very strategic.

asr-000265
00:36:46.160 --> 00:36:51.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because these are the areas that there's a big chance of making a discovery, correct?

asr-000266
00:36:51.020 --> 00:36:51.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes.

asr-000267
00:36:53.220 --> 00:36:57.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So you want to be sure that this item is secured in the budget, right?

asr-000268
00:36:57.320 --> 00:37:02.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: This is not an additional budget you're asking for. It's already in the NEP.

asr-000269
00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:02.820
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Yes, ma'am.

asr-000270
00:37:02.820 --> 00:37:03.320
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Okay.

asr-000271
00:37:03.540 --> 00:37:10.900
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: And just briefly, Sandy, our in-house expert on this, can explain why.

asr-000272
00:37:10.900 --> 00:37:15.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes, explain it very quickly on the record because our briefing is not live.

asr-000273
00:37:16.060 --> 00:37:21.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I want people to know that we're investing in this kind of exploration.

asr-000274
00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:22.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yes.

asr-000275
00:37:23.220 --> 00:37:31.300
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: So, first point really is [unclear] po ng department kung saan natin dadalhin itong bagong acquisition ng data.

asr-000276
00:37:31.960 --> 00:37:37.640
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: So, for the information, the last major exercise like this was in the 80s

asr-000277
00:37:37.640 --> 00:37:42.260
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: na nag-acquire ng data ang Philippine government over our basins.

asr-000278
00:37:42.600 --> 00:37:45.800
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: And it was funded through a World Bank loan.

asr-000279
00:37:45.800 --> 00:37:52.580
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: So, major milestone that after so many decades, we are again investing.

asr-000280
00:37:53.220 --> 00:37:54.740
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: In our own basins.

asr-000281
00:37:55.580 --> 00:38:07.060
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: The main criteria why we picked these basins is parang nakalimutan sila because the decision in the 70s and 80s was that these areas were gas-prone.

asr-000282
00:38:08.280 --> 00:38:13.020
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: At that time, natural gas po ay mahirap gawing commercial.

asr-000283
00:38:13.580 --> 00:38:14.820
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Walang masyadong bumibili.

asr-000284
00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:22.880
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: When gas became a very valuable commodity beginning in the 2000s and up to the present time.

asr-000285
00:38:22.880 --> 00:38:30.440
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: And in fact, kailangan ng Pilipinas, [unclear] namin itong mga areas na ito, nakalimutan dahil gas-prone daw.

asr-000286
00:38:30.880 --> 00:38:39.600
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: But it could really matter to the future of the country if we find more indigenous gas in this what we call forgotten areas.

asr-000287
00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:40.140
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Thank you po.

asr-000288
00:38:40.900 --> 00:38:41.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you for that.

asr-000289
00:38:41.780 --> 00:38:51.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi I remember when I sponsored our bill on NatGas, we put on record that sadly,

asr-000290
00:38:51.140 --> 00:38:57.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the height of exploration, investment was in the 70s.

asr-000291
00:38:58.180 --> 00:38:59.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, hindi na ho naulit yun.

asr-000292
00:38:59.920 --> 00:39:05.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, you're tying in that information we have na 80s pala yung last data collection.

asr-000293
00:39:06.560 --> 00:39:14.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But it makes sense that at that time, since hindi pa NatGas yung uso, hindi muna tinuloy.

asr-000294
00:39:14.500 --> 00:39:20.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Tapos ngayon, kailangan na nating—NatGas is really a very valuable commodity now.

asr-000295
00:39:20.320 --> 00:39:21.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, now's a good time.

asr-000296
00:39:21.140 --> 00:39:25.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For this to really be, for this to be the focus.

asr-000297
00:39:25.520 --> 00:39:25.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000298
00:39:26.060 --> 00:39:33.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But later on, you'll also mention the development also and what, exploration for geothermal, no?

asr-000299
00:39:33.780 --> 00:39:36.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi malaki din yung investment natin dati.

asr-000300
00:39:37.100 --> 00:39:39.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, later on, I think that's part of your presentation naman.

asr-000301
00:39:41.080 --> 00:39:43.480
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Madam Chair, if I may, one last point.

asr-000302
00:39:43.920 --> 00:39:49.080
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Actually, when we talk to investors, malaking push din yung nangyari sa NatGas law.

asr-000303
00:39:49.300 --> 00:39:50.980
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Because, ang nangyari doon,

asr-000304
00:39:51.140 --> 00:39:54.800
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: it really bridged the gap between yung upstream, yung pag-explore,

asr-000305
00:39:55.160 --> 00:39:56.960
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: and saan natin ibebenta.

asr-000306
00:39:57.720 --> 00:40:01.000
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: What happened with our NatGas law was the market was assured

asr-000307
00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:05.780
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: because we said in the law that preference ang indigenous gas.

asr-000308
00:40:05.940 --> 00:40:09.560
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: So, very important factor when we go out and meet the investors.

asr-000309
00:40:09.980 --> 00:40:10.400
DOE Undersecretary Alessandro O. Sales: Thank you po.

asr-000310
00:40:10.400 --> 00:40:16.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And for those just following now, I remember the discussion was,

asr-000311
00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:20.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the emphasis here, the reality here is it's such a big investment because,

asr-000312
00:40:20.560 --> 00:40:24.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: yung investors tataya, may makahanap ka ba?

asr-000313
00:40:25.320 --> 00:40:26.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hindi tayo sure, di ba?

asr-000314
00:40:26.400 --> 00:40:27.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hindi tayo sure.

asr-000315
00:40:27.680 --> 00:40:29.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they may spend a lot and not get anything.

asr-000316
00:40:30.240 --> 00:40:33.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, to be able to tell them that if you do find gas,

asr-000317
00:40:33.560 --> 00:40:38.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: priority in the Philippines to purchase their own indigenous gas versus yung imported.

asr-000318
00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:39.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Importante yun.

asr-000319
00:40:39.900 --> 00:40:43.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi, for investors, yun ang hinahanap nila na ano yung return of investment.

asr-000320
00:40:44.180 --> 00:40:46.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pwede kasing zero talaga eh kung walang makita.

asr-000321
00:40:46.820 --> 00:40:48.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But, at least we're saying, pag may nakita,

asr-000322
00:40:48.600 --> 00:40:50.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: then, I mean,

asr-000323
00:40:50.100 --> 00:40:53.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: those who are investing are in the industry naman eh.

asr-000324
00:40:53.120 --> 00:40:54.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, they know the risk.

asr-000325
00:40:54.420 --> 00:40:57.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But, to be assured that there will be a buyer is a big thing.

asr-000326
00:40:58.300 --> 00:40:59.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yeah.

asr-000327
00:40:59.180 --> 00:41:03.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I'm glad that you have this investment now for this project to proceed.

