asr-000538
00:50:50.840 --> 00:50:55.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, let's get this going and let's try to maintain na talaga.

asr-000539
00:50:55.560 --> 00:50:58.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And yeah, the idea is later on when they're so good, sila naman...

asr-000540
00:50:58.560 --> 00:50:59.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Well, nangyari na nga.

asr-000541
00:50:59.560 --> 00:51:00.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Umalis na lahat dati.

asr-000542
00:51:00.880 --> 00:51:02.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, let's rebuild again.

asr-000543
00:51:03.080 --> 00:51:03.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000544
00:51:03.740 --> 00:51:04.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, we'll go now.

asr-000545
00:51:04.880 --> 00:51:08.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think, wait, before I go to Attorney Juan, just very quick questions.

asr-000546
00:51:08.500 --> 00:51:09.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Very quick.

asr-000547
00:51:11.000 --> 00:51:12.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What's our current energy mix?

asr-000548
00:51:17.440 --> 00:51:19.720
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: We are currently coal.

asr-000549
00:51:19.720 --> 00:51:20.720
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Is about 62%.

asr-000550
00:51:20.840 --> 00:51:21.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000551
00:51:22.040 --> 00:51:24.680
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And then, renewables is about 25%.

asr-000552
00:51:24.680 --> 00:51:30.500
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And then, you have the rest, the oil and gas and so on, as well as the others.

asr-000553
00:51:30.680 --> 00:51:34.540
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And also, BES, battery energy storage system.

asr-000554
00:51:35.100 --> 00:51:39.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, with the top two, that's already equivalent to 87%, no?

asr-000555
00:51:40.380 --> 00:51:45.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I'll give you a minute to tell me how RE is doing.

asr-000556
00:51:45.000 --> 00:51:50.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because we do know that RE use is going up and even the cost of RE is going down.

asr-000557
00:51:50.520 --> 00:51:50.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, can you...

asr-000558
00:51:50.720 --> 00:51:53.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Can you make your little, you know, make that statement about it?

asr-000559
00:51:53.860 --> 00:51:57.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because this is what so many environmentalists have been waiting to happen.

asr-000560
00:51:57.940 --> 00:51:59.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And it has happened in our lifetime.

asr-000561
00:52:01.200 --> 00:52:01.660
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Madam Chair.

asr-000562
00:52:02.020 --> 00:52:04.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Let me just acknowledge Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-000563
00:52:05.020 --> 00:52:08.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sir, I'll give you a minute to make an opening statement if you want.

asr-000564
00:52:08.260 --> 00:52:09.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll just let her finish this question.

asr-000565
00:52:10.020 --> 00:52:10.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead.

asr-000566
00:52:10.680 --> 00:52:13.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I don't have any opening statement, Madam Chair.

asr-000567
00:52:13.920 --> 00:52:14.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sige.

asr-000568
00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:16.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, go ahead and answer the question lang.

asr-000569
00:52:16.640 --> 00:52:19.040
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Madam Chair, from 2022 to 2024,

asr-000570
00:52:19.040 --> 00:52:24.720
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: our renewable energy in the generation mix in megawatt hours was 22%.

asr-000571
00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:28.940
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Last year, 2025, it jumped to 25%.

asr-000572
00:52:28.940 --> 00:52:30.740
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: It's a 3% increase.

asr-000573
00:52:31.300 --> 00:52:36.580
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: So, we figured based on our plans and the green energy auction results,

asr-000574
00:52:37.300 --> 00:52:42.600
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: by 2030, we will reach 35% of renewable energy in the generation mix.

asr-000575
00:52:44.680 --> 00:52:46.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And that's the target?

asr-000576
00:52:46.820 --> 00:52:47.340
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Yes, ma'am.

asr-000577
00:52:47.340 --> 00:52:47.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000578
00:52:47.980 --> 00:52:48.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And in terms of pricing,

asr-000580
00:52:49.700 --> 00:52:50.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: banggitin mo na,

asr-000581
00:52:50.840 --> 00:52:52.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kasi on record.

asr-000582
00:52:52.460 --> 00:52:55.140
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Dati po yung coal, mas mura siya kesa sa solar.

asr-000583
00:52:55.520 --> 00:52:58.120
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Ngayon, solar is cheaper than coal already.

asr-000584
00:52:59.020 --> 00:52:59.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I'll repeat.

asr-000585
00:53:00.020 --> 00:53:02.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Solar is now cheaper than coal.

asr-000586
00:53:02.360 --> 00:53:08.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, in our desire to push for more RE, more renewables, more sustainable,

asr-000587
00:53:09.000 --> 00:53:15.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we are on track and it should happen because hindi na madaling sabihin na

asr-000588
00:53:15.200 --> 00:53:17.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: mas mura ang coal, kailangan natin umasa sa coal.

asr-000589
00:53:17.720 --> 00:53:19.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And can you also add to the discussion?

asr-000590
00:53:19.040 --> 00:53:21.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, people understand, no?

asr-000591
00:53:21.700 --> 00:53:25.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because it's very rare that you get a full picture.

asr-000592
00:53:25.840 --> 00:53:31.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: One of the reasons why RE, renewable energy, was difficult to push was because of the storage.

asr-000593
00:53:32.640 --> 00:53:36.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, kung walang araw, hindi mo na-store yung na-collect mong energy,

asr-000594
00:53:36.800 --> 00:53:38.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: wala kang magagamit, diba?

asr-000595
00:53:38.160 --> 00:53:40.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, hindi siya nagagamit for base load.

asr-000596
00:53:41.060 --> 00:53:47.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But now, maybe you can update us on what is the scenario now with the batteries?

asr-000597
00:53:49.040 --> 00:53:52.360
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Today, even households can have solar and battery.

asr-000598
00:53:52.780 --> 00:53:55.020
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Solar para mag-charge siya ng battery.

asr-000599
00:53:55.180 --> 00:53:57.100
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Para pati sa gabi, renewable siya.

asr-000600
00:53:57.260 --> 00:54:02.360
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Because battery prices have gone down by 90% in the past 10 years.

asr-000601
00:54:02.520 --> 00:54:02.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000602
00:54:03.080 --> 00:54:07.220
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And Madam Chair, to also add, yung pong ating mga renewables ngayon,

asr-000603
00:54:07.360 --> 00:54:10.760
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: people are worried na ang mahal naman niyang bagong technology na yan.

asr-000604
00:54:11.060 --> 00:54:17.000
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: I would like to remind people that when we started solar as fit in 2015,

asr-000605
00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:19.000
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: the price was ₱9.68

asr-000606
00:54:19.560 --> 00:54:20.360
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: per kilowatt hour.

asr-000607
00:54:20.620 --> 00:54:20.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000608
00:54:21.040 --> 00:54:22.000
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And today, it's 4.5.

asr-000609
00:54:22.680 --> 00:54:23.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Wow.

asr-000610
00:54:23.500 --> 00:54:27.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, from 9.68 to 4.5.

asr-000611
00:54:27.240 --> 00:54:27.960
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: 4.5.

asr-000612
00:54:28.200 --> 00:54:33.300
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: So, we would like to encourage people not to be afraid of the initial high price of new technologies

asr-000613
00:54:33.300 --> 00:54:35.320
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: because it will really go down.

asr-000614
00:54:35.540 --> 00:54:37.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay. Thank you for that, ma'am.

asr-000615
00:54:38.280 --> 00:54:39.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, energy mix.

asr-000616
00:54:39.640 --> 00:54:42.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, my other question is, what's the fastest growing?

asr-000617
00:54:43.080 --> 00:54:43.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, solar na nga.

asr-000618
00:54:44.400 --> 00:54:44.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Solar.

asr-000619
00:54:44.740 --> 00:54:48.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yung aasahan ko sana dyan is geothermal din, no?

asr-000620
00:54:48.240 --> 00:54:48.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sana.

asr-000621
00:54:48.520 --> 00:54:49.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sana. Pero hindi pa.

asr-000622
00:54:49.880 --> 00:54:54.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi sabi niyo, yung presentation kanina is binabalik pa lang natin ulit eh.

asr-000623
00:54:56.080 --> 00:55:00.260
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: We are going to borrow money from Asian Development Bank,

asr-000624
00:55:00.340 --> 00:55:06.000
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: $170 million to de-risk the exploration of wells for geothermal.

asr-000625
00:55:06.460 --> 00:55:08.780
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Yun po kasi yung pinaka-risky part eh.

asr-000626
00:55:09.220 --> 00:55:12.580
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Kailangan mong mag-drill ng tatlong wells, $6 to $8 million each.

asr-000627
00:55:12.840 --> 00:55:13.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000628
00:55:13.120 --> 00:55:15.240
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Lahat sila successful bago mo sabihin na,

asr-000629
00:55:15.660 --> 00:55:16.840
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: bakit di ako mag-drill dito?

asr-000630
00:55:17.140 --> 00:55:17.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000631
00:55:17.320 --> 00:55:22.140
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: And since 2012, when we sold our geothermal plants,

asr-000632
00:55:22.420 --> 00:55:24.300
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: we have not had greenfield.

asr-000633
00:55:24.400 --> 00:55:25.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Since 2012.

asr-000634
00:55:26.040 --> 00:55:28.240
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Because the private sector is afraid of the risk.

asr-000635
00:55:28.840 --> 00:55:32.500
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: So, the geothermal de-risking facility that we are borrowing from ADB

asr-000636
00:55:32.500 --> 00:55:37.040
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: will basically say, 50% of the risk will be taken by the government.

asr-000637
00:55:37.520 --> 00:55:42.840
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: So, land bank, our partner, will lend money for exploration, drilling wells.

asr-000638
00:55:43.120 --> 00:55:43.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000639
00:55:43.440 --> 00:55:46.640
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: If the geothermal developer is successful,

asr-000640
00:55:47.320 --> 00:55:48.820
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: repay land bank.

asr-000641
00:55:49.060 --> 00:55:51.940
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: If they're not successful, it's a grant from the Philippine government.

asr-000642
00:55:52.620 --> 00:55:56.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, tumaya ka, but 50% of that is secure ka.

asr-000643
00:55:57.060 --> 00:56:01.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yung risk mo is just 50%.

asr-000644
00:56:01.440 --> 00:56:06.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And it's a loan from ADB by the government?

asr-000645
00:56:06.760 --> 00:56:07.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Is that what it is?

asr-000646
00:56:07.660 --> 00:56:09.040
DOE Undersecretary Rowena Cristina L. Guevara: Yes. Sovereign guaranteed loan.

asr-000647
00:56:09.140 --> 00:56:11.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay. So, that means, basically, yung government yung tumataya.

asr-000648
00:56:11.760 --> 00:56:15.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's just that tinulungan tayo ng ADB to provide the funding.

asr-000649
00:56:16.160 --> 00:56:16.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-000650
00:56:17.320 --> 00:56:20.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, just for your information, Senator Tulfo,

asr-000651
00:56:21.320 --> 00:56:22.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: there are just two presentations.

asr-000652
00:56:22.980 --> 00:56:24.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The first one is done by DOE.

asr-000653
00:56:25.080 --> 00:56:30.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The second one is going to be presented to us by Attorney Juan for ERC.

asr-000654
00:56:30.420 --> 00:56:32.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, after that, I'll open it to questions.

asr-000655
00:56:32.440 --> 00:56:33.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, are you okay with that?

asr-000656
00:56:33.560 --> 00:56:34.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Dalawa lang naman tayo, no?

asr-000657
00:56:35.180 --> 00:56:35.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yes, Madam Chair.

asr-000658
00:56:36.460 --> 00:56:39.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay. So, Attorney Juan, please proceed. Thank you.

asr-000659
00:56:41.220 --> 00:56:46.200
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Thank you, Madam Chair, Honorable Senator Erwin Tulfo,

asr-000660
00:56:46.200 --> 00:56:51.380
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and my Secretary Sharon Garin, and my colleagues in the Energy Family.

asr-000661
00:56:51.900 --> 00:56:55.900
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: I am Attorney Juan, Chairperson and CEO of the ERC.

asr-000662
00:56:56.980 --> 00:57:03.460
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And with me are the Commissioners of ERC, Commissioner Floresinda Baldo-Digal,

asr-000663
00:57:04.200 --> 00:57:08.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Commissioner Amante Liberato, and Commissioner Paris Real.

asr-000664
00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:15.500
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Our mandate in EPIRA is very clear, and that is to promote competition,

asr-000665
00:57:15.500 --> 00:57:16.180
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: ensure

asr-000666
00:57:16.200 --> 00:57:19.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: consumer choice, protect consumer interests,

asr-000667
00:57:19.780 --> 00:57:24.220
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and keep retail rates based on prudent and reasonable cost recovery,

asr-000668
00:57:24.640 --> 00:57:27.380
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and penalize abuse of market power.

asr-000669
00:57:28.380 --> 00:57:28.760
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Slide three.

asr-000670
00:57:29.740 --> 00:57:33.940
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: We regulate the full electricity value chain, the regulated sectors,

asr-000671
00:57:34.360 --> 00:57:39.280
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: transmission and distribution, and the competitive sector generation and supply.

asr-000672
00:57:39.280 --> 00:57:45.280
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So, there can be better appreciation of the following slides as regards the ERC accomplishments

asr-000673
00:57:46.200 --> 00:57:52.540
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Let me just describe briefly how we regulate the transmission and distribution sector.

asr-000674
00:57:52.540 --> 00:58:00.160
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Basically, we set the rates and performance standards for our transmission utility, the NGCP,

asr-000675
00:58:00.600 --> 00:58:07.560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and our distribution utilities, both the private utilities and the electric cooperatives.

asr-000676
00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:14.500
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: For our monitoring and oversight over the competitive sector, namely the generation and supply,

asr-000677
00:58:14.500 --> 00:58:15.500
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: we basically license it.

asr-000678
00:58:16.200 --> 00:58:30.080
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: These entities, the generation companies, through the issuance of certificates of compliance, as well as license the retail electricity suppliers through the issuance of the RES licenses to them.

asr-000679
00:58:30.080 --> 00:58:46.080
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: At the same time, we issue regulations that will govern the sector short of setting or regulating the prices at which these entities offer to their respective customers.

asr-000680
00:58:46.080 --> 00:58:59.860
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Except that for generation companies that are selling to distribution utilities for their captive market, we review the power supply agreements.

asr-000681
00:59:00.080 --> 00:59:30.060
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: that they enter into, as well as for ancillary service providers that are offering ancillary services to the transmission service provider. We likewise review and approve the ancillary service procurement agreements or ASPAs that they enter into. Slide four: the industry we regulate is valued at ₱4.19 trillion, with the DOE projecting around

asr-000682
00:59:30.080 --> 01:00:00.060
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: ₱20 to ₱31 trillion in investment needs through 2050, and with this it is anticipated that 1.8 million jobs will be created. So this is the scale of the energy sector that our proposed budget of ₱940 million must support. Next slide, the ERC has awoken from its slumber: 5,149 decisions

asr-000683
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:09.480
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and orders issued in the period which is more than double the 2,411 issued in the same months

asr-000684
01:00:09.480 --> 01:00:16.820
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: a year earlier. With the National Lifeline Subsidy Program that ERC developed last year

asr-000685
01:00:16.820 --> 01:00:25.420
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: in consultation with the DOE and the DSWD, lifeline rate subsidy coverage is up 85.33 percent.

asr-000686
01:00:25.420 --> 01:00:33.780
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: It now reaches 620,000 qualified marginalized end users. Net metering registrations are up

asr-000687
01:00:33.780 --> 01:00:42.240
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: 51.77 percent under the streamlined licensing procedures that ERC implemented also last year.

asr-000688
01:00:42.920 --> 01:00:50.660
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Worthy to mention also is the completed rate reset of NGCP both for the fourth regulatory period

asr-000689
01:00:50.660 --> 01:00:55.400
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: and the fifth regulatory period. This happened in 2024.

asr-000690
01:00:55.420 --> 01:01:00.620
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And this happened after more than a decade of delays.

asr-000691
01:01:01.580 --> 01:01:12.500
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: And together with the rate reset of NGCP was the approval of 1,602 CAPEX projects worth 290 billion.

asr-000692
01:01:13.040 --> 01:01:13.560
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: Next slide.

asr-000693
01:01:14.440 --> 01:01:21.240
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: The ERC also approved 71.3 billion in refunds as of August 2026.

asr-000694
01:01:21.240 --> 01:01:25.140
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: More than triple the 21.3 billion.

asr-000695
01:01:25.420 --> 01:01:34.480
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: A year earlier, including the 69.95 billion that Meralco was asked to refund

asr-000696
01:01:34.480 --> 01:01:44.840
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: under the true-up mechanism or the actual weighted average tariff mechanism that ERC devised

asr-000697
01:01:44.840 --> 01:01:55.280
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: so it can address the period during which there were no rate reset that was conducted for our private distribution.

asr-000698
01:01:55.420 --> 01:02:04.160
ERC Chairperson and CEO Francis Saturnino C. Juan: So it is Meralco that was directed but soon because the ERC also directed other private distribution utilities

asr-000699
01:02:04.160 --> 01:02:15.300
