Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we benefit

asr-004376
03:28:35.680 --> 03:28:37.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: from it. So dapat pababain pa

asr-004377
03:28:37.340 --> 03:28:38.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: natin to the consumer.

asr-004378
03:28:39.760 --> 03:28:41.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero yung affordable,

asr-004379
03:28:42.800 --> 03:28:43.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: medyo dyan

asr-004380
03:28:43.700 --> 03:28:44.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: pa tayo pwedeng

asr-004381
03:28:44.700 --> 03:28:46.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: mag-improve

asr-004382
03:28:46.620 --> 03:28:47.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kasi yung mix,

asr-004383
03:28:47.680 --> 03:28:49.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: nga natin, it's not purely

asr-004384
03:28:49.460 --> 03:28:51.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: renewable. If it was purely renewable, then

asr-004385
03:28:51.540 --> 03:28:53.520
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we're on track for clean and affordable,

asr-004386
03:28:53.740 --> 03:28:55.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: correct? But it is not purely

asr-004387
03:28:55.560 --> 03:28:57.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: renewable. We still have 62%

asr-004388
03:28:57.400 --> 03:28:59.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: of coal. So

asr-004389
03:28:59.500 --> 03:29:01.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and then the remaining balance

asr-004390
03:29:01.700 --> 03:29:03.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: is, what, mga 17%

asr-004391
03:29:03.540 --> 03:29:05.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: of others. So we can still

asr-004392
03:29:05.620 --> 03:29:06.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: improve on that.

asr-004393
03:29:11.340 --> 03:29:13.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: For energy security, it's not enough

asr-004394
03:29:13.680 --> 03:29:15.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that we are in survival mode, no?

asr-004395
03:29:15.360 --> 03:29:17.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We have to really look into the future.

asr-004396
03:29:17.180 --> 03:29:19.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I need us to see

asr-004397
03:29:19.280 --> 03:29:21.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and I'd like you to submit this to me.

asr-004398
03:29:21.260 --> 03:29:21.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nothing fancy,

asr-004399
03:29:22.700 --> 03:29:24.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because you do have the energy plan.

asr-004400
03:29:25.720 --> 03:29:27.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 10, 20, 30,

asr-004401
03:29:27.540 --> 03:29:29.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 50 years, because if you haven't

asr-004402
03:29:29.120 --> 03:29:30.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: heard me say this before,

asr-004403
03:29:31.080 --> 03:29:33.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: there are countries that have a plan

asr-004404
03:29:33.360 --> 03:29:35.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: for seven generations

asr-004405
03:29:35.340 --> 03:29:36.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: to come.

asr-004406
03:29:37.360 --> 03:29:39.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So kahit hindi naman siguro seven generations,

asr-004407
03:29:39.320 --> 03:29:40.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kahit two to three,

asr-004408
03:29:40.640 --> 03:29:43.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: hindi na talaga natin naabutan yun, but siguro

asr-004409
03:29:43.180 --> 03:29:44.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that's what our grandchildren,

asr-004410
03:29:44.640 --> 03:29:46.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: something like that.

asr-004411
03:29:47.180 --> 03:29:48.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's being done.

asr-004412
03:29:48.280 --> 03:29:51.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So it's not something I'm inventing.

asr-004413
03:29:51.220 --> 03:29:53.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That is a practice of countries that

asr-004414
03:29:53.060 --> 03:29:54.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: are truly

asr-004415
03:29:54.080 --> 03:29:57.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: future-proofing their country.

asr-004416
03:29:57.920 --> 03:29:58.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So

asr-004417
03:30:00.000 --> 03:30:19.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: By investing in long-term security, then we'll have to make tough decisions. That's for sure. And we'll have to allocate limited funds. That's also sure that limited lang yung funds natin. But these are for the programs that will ensure that the average Filipino has, again, access to clean and affordable energy.

asr-004418
03:30:19.760 --> 03:30:30.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, on that note, Mr. President, I am happy to [unclear] siguro, no? Wala nang? Yes, Secretary.

asr-004419
03:30:30.240 --> 03:30:43.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Before you wrap up, I know we have sent a letter with all the possible requests for funding. This includes the system loss for NEA and all that.

asr-004420
03:30:43.660 --> 03:30:49.660
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: But as a priority, Madam Chair, we would rather have?

asr-004421
03:30:49.760 --> 03:30:56.440
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: If there's available funding, then that the increase in the ERC funding be done.

asr-004422
03:30:56.580 --> 03:31:04.480
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Because sila yung kailangan nila ng faster resolution of all the issues will help also.

asr-004423
03:31:04.480 --> 03:31:07.020
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's the 720 million. We noted that.

asr-004424
03:31:07.060 --> 03:31:07.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yun lang yung…

asr-004425
03:31:07.660 --> 03:31:11.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And kayang-kaya ni SP yan, saka ni Chairman.

asr-004426
03:31:11.880 --> 03:31:18.380
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: We'll give way to them first. Kung may natirapay, then we can request.

asr-004427
03:31:18.380 --> 03:31:19.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Quick question lang.

asr-004428
03:31:19.280 --> 03:31:22.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung system loss, non-technical yun sa NEA?

asr-004429
03:31:22.320 --> 03:31:23.160
DOE Secretary Sharon S. Garin: Non-technical, yeah.

asr-004430
03:31:23.320 --> 03:31:27.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Non-technical. And so, the concept, gobyerno mag-absorb yung non-technical?

asr-004431
03:31:29.400 --> 03:31:33.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Saka pa-absorb rin ng private sector sa atin, private DU sa atin.

asr-004432
03:31:34.740 --> 03:31:35.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Libre nga.

asr-004433
03:31:36.040 --> 03:31:45.600
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: SP, the non-technical system loss fund request was to add up to the equity loan facility of NEA

asr-004434
03:31:45.600 --> 03:31:49.100
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: to extend loans to electric cooperatives.

asr-004435
03:31:49.280 --> 03:31:58.300
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Hindi po subsidy yun. Yun po ay pandagdag sa equity loan namin para maipautang namin sa mga electric cooperatives

asr-004436
03:31:58.300 --> 03:32:03.940
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: to upgrade their facilities mainly on their metering requirements.

asr-004437
03:32:06.040 --> 03:32:10.360
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: So, we found it palatable na hindi po namin ibibigay as a subsidy.

asr-004438
03:32:10.800 --> 03:32:18.200
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Pautangin po nila as their CAPEX requirement to upgrade their facility para mawala ho yung non-technical system loss.

asr-004439
03:32:18.200 --> 03:32:18.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Non-technical yun.

asr-004440
03:32:18.640 --> 03:32:20.240
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Sa non-technical po.

asr-004441
03:32:20.580 --> 03:32:22.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Non-technical is pilferage, di ba?

asr-004442
03:32:22.660 --> 03:32:33.080
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Well, nung previous hearings po, prinisinta namin, meron po kasi kaming isang case in point na isang electric cooperative

asr-004443
03:32:33.080 --> 03:32:37.340
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: na napakataas ng system loss, total system loss.

asr-004444
03:32:37.460 --> 03:32:40.660
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: And we identified po, much of that is non-technical pilferage.

asr-004445
03:32:41.460 --> 03:32:44.660
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: I am talking about referring to Zamboanga City Electric Cooperative.

asr-004446
03:32:44.660 --> 03:32:48.600
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: So, when we implemented it,

asr-004447
03:32:48.640 --> 03:32:56.700
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: a pilot plan from January to July, from 23%, we brought it down to 13%.

asr-004448
03:32:56.700 --> 03:33:05.000
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Ang ginawa lang ho namin, hinanap lang ho namin yung walang metro at saka yung mga koneksyon na iligal, minetrohan ho namin.

asr-004449
03:33:05.180 --> 03:33:09.720
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: So, the same formula po, yun ang gagawin ho namin sa mga ibang electric cooperative.

asr-004450
03:33:10.660 --> 03:33:15.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pilferage, in other words, lalagyan ng metro para magbayad.

asr-004451
03:33:15.560 --> 03:33:15.820
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Opo.

asr-004452
03:33:15.820 --> 03:33:15.960
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Opo.

asr-004453
03:33:16.260 --> 03:33:16.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-004454
03:33:17.480 --> 03:33:18.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ganun kasimple lang.

asr-004455
03:33:18.400 --> 03:33:18.620
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Ganun.

asr-004456
03:33:18.640 --> 03:33:19.300
NEA Administrator Antonio Mariano C. Almeda: Ganun kasimple lang.

asr-004457
03:33:19.440 --> 03:33:19.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-004458
03:33:19.800 --> 03:33:20.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you.

